<section id="publications" class="py-20 sm:py-28 border-t border-subtle">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 sm:px-6">
    <h2 class="section-heading mb-10">Publications</h2>

    <article class="rounded-2xl border border-subtle bg-surface p-6 sm:p-8 hover:border-accent-300 dark:hover:border-accent-700 transition-colors">
      <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
        <div class="flex-shrink-0 mt-1">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-accent-100 dark:bg-accent-900/40 flex items-center justify-center">
            <svg class="h-5 w-5 text-accent-600 dark:text-accent-400" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12h6m-6 4h6m2 5H7a2 2 0 01-2-2V5a2 2 0 012-2h5.586a1 1 0 01.707.293l5.414 5.414a1 1 0 01.293.707V19a2 2 0 01-2 2z" />
            </svg>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex-1 min-w-0">
          <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 mb-2">
            <span class="tag">Privacy / ML</span>
            <span class="text-xs text-muted">PoPETs 2021</span>
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold leading-snug mb-2">
            A First Look at Private Communications in Video Games using Visual Features
          </h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-muted mb-3">
            A. Wajid, N. Kamal, M. Sharjeel, R. M. Sheikh, <strong>H. B. Wasim</strong>, M. H. Ali, W. Hussain, F. Zaffar.
            <br />
            <em>Proceedings on Privacy Enhancing Technologies (PoPETs)</em>, 2021(3), pp. 433–452.
          </p>
          <p class="text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed">
            Investigated covert communication channels within video game environments using visual feature extraction
            and ML-based classification — an end-to-end study from data labeling and feature engineering through
            model training and evaluation.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
